# Auto commit + push

After finishing a meaningful change set for this project:

1. Commit all relevant files with a concise message focused on why.
2. Push to `origin` on the current branch immediately.
3. Do not wait for the user to say "commit" or "push".

Follow the existing git safety protocol (no force push to main/master, no config changes, no secrets in commits). If push fails due to auth, report it and stop.
